"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[82622],{482622:e=>{e.exports='### Failure Category Guidance\n\nWhen diagnosing failures, refer to these common categories and their typical patterns:\n\n**Category A: Dependency & Environment Build Failures**\n- **DEPENDENCY_CONFLICT (NumPy/pandas)**: "numpy.dtype size changed", "ValueError: numpy.ndarray size changed", "_ARRAY_API not found"\n  - **CRITICAL**: NumPy 2.0+ is incompatible with pandas <2.2.2 (causes "served entity creation aborted")\n  - Fix: Pin `numpy<2.0` in requirements.txt OR upgrade `pandas>=2.2.2`\n- **DEPENDENCY_CONFLICT**: "Cannot install X and Y because these package versions have conflicting dependencies"\n  - Fix: Pin compatible versions, use pip-tools to resolve conflicts, check package compatibility matrix\n- **MISSING_PACKAGE**: "No matching distribution found for package-name", "Could not find a version that satisfies"\n  - Fix: Verify package name/version exists on PyPI, check for typos, configure --extra-index-url for private repos\n- **PYTHON_VERSION_MISMATCH**: "Python version X is not compatible", "requires Python >=3.11"\n  - Fix: Update python_version in MLmodel or use compatible package versions\n- **MISSING_SYSTEM_LIBRARY**: "libcuda.so: cannot open shared object file", "fatal error: cuda.h: No such file"\n  - Fix: Use Databricks-provided GPU base images with CUDA pre-installed, ensure workload_type=GPU_*\n- **ABI_INCOMPATIBILITY**: "ABI tag mismatch", "incompatible with this Python", "wrong ELF class"\n  - Fix: Rebuild packages for target platform, ensure wheels match Python version and architecture (manylinux)\n\n**Category B: Model Artifact & Packaging Errors**\n- **MISSING_ENVIRONMENT_FILE**: "MLmodel file not found"\n  - Fix: Re-log model ensuring all artifacts are included\n- **MISSING_ARTIFACT**: "model.pkl not found", "artifact does not exist", "No such file or directory" (model files)\n  - **CRITICAL**: Model artifacts missing from Unity Catalog registry\n  - Fix: Verify model logging and Unity Catalog permissions. Check model was logged with all required files.\n- **INVALID_MODEL_FORMAT**: "MLmodel validation failed", "Schema version not supported"\n  - Fix: Re-log model with current MLflow version. Ensure model signature is defined.\n- **ARTIFACT_LOADING_FAILURE**: "artifact corrupt", "download failed", "checksum mismatch"\n  - Escalate: Artifact corruption or download failure requires infrastructure investigation\n- **DISK_SPACE_EXHAUSTED**: "No space left on device", "Disk quota exceeded", "/tmp is full"\n  - **CRITICAL**: Disk space exhaustion (common with excessive MLflow artifacts)\n  - Fix: Reduce model/artifact size. Clear temporary files. Reduce logging size.\n\n**Category C: Container Startup & Initialization Failures**\n- **IMPORT_ERROR**: "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'X\'", "ImportError", "cannot import name", "SyntaxError", "NameError", "AttributeError"\n  - Fix: Add missing package to requirements.txt. Check for package version API mismatches. Test model locally.\n- **OUT_OF_MEMORY**: "OutOfMemoryError", "OOMKilled", "MemoryError"\n  - Fix: Optimize model memory usage (reduce batch size, use smaller model variant, enable memory-efficient loading). Note: workload_size controls concurrency, NOT memory per model.\n- **MISSING_ENV_VAR**: "Environment variable \'X\' is required but not set", "KeyError" (environment variables)\n  - Fix: Set environment variable in endpoint config or use secrets\n- **MISSING_SECRET**: "Secret not found", "secret scope not accessible"\n  - Fix: Grant READ permission on secret scope to endpoint service principal\n- **IDENTITY_MISCONFIGURATION (Credentials)**: "Credentials failed to generate", "credential deployment failed", "CredentialDeploymentFailed"\n  - **CRITICAL**: Backend ServedModelState.CredentialDeploymentFailed - credentials for feature serving failed\n  - Escalate: Verify Unity Catalog access and OAuth configuration. Contact support if persists.\n- **SERVER_STARTUP_FAILURE (Feature Store)**: "Feature store setup failed", "online table not ready", "FeatureSpec does not exist"\n  - **CRITICAL**: Backend ServedModelState.FeatureStoreSetupFailed - online feature store setup failed\n  - Fix: Verify online tables have ONLINE_CONTINUOUS_UPDATE status. Check Unity Catalog permissions on feature tables.\n- **SERVER_STARTUP_FAILURE (Database)**: "Connection refused database", "Could not connect to database", "database connection timeout"\n  - Fix: Cannot connect to database for feature serving. Verify online tables accessible. Check network policies.\n- **SERVER_STARTUP_FAILURE (Server Init)**: "uvicorn failed", "gunicorn failed", "server startup failed", "Flask failed to start"\n  - Fix: Check service logs for stack trace. Verify server code in custom model. Test locally with mlflow models serve.\n- **SERVER_STARTUP_FAILURE (Build Timeout)**: "Build timed out", "Container build timeout", "Image build exceeded minutes"\n  - **CRITICAL**: Build exceeded timeout (30min CPU, 60min GPU S/M, 120min GPU L)\n  - Fix: Optimize dependency installation, reduce artifacts, use pre-built wheels\n- **SERVER_STARTUP_FAILURE (Request Timeout)**: "Request timed out", "Timed out while evaluating", "predict timeout"\n  - Model initialization timeout on first request (297s hard limit)\n  - Fix: Optimize model loading code or enable autoscaling to avoid cold starts\n- **SERVER_STARTUP_FAILURE (Exit Code)**: "exit with code 137", "Exit code: 1", "Container exit code"\n  - Exit codes: 137=OOMKilled, 1=general error, 2=misuse, 126=cannot execute, 127=command not found\n  - Fix: Check service logs for stack trace. Exit code 137 indicates OOM - optimize model memory usage, reduce initialization memory footprint.\n- **HEALTH_CHECK_FAILURE**: "Health check failed: /health returned 500", "Readiness probe failed"\n  - Fix: Check model server logs for initialization errors. Verify model loads successfully.\n- **GPU_RUNTIME_MISMATCH**: "CUDA error", "cuDNN error", "No CUDA-capable device", "CUDA version mismatch"\n  - Fix: Ensure workload_type=GPU_*. Use PyTorch/TensorFlow with matching CUDA version.\n\n**Category D: Permissions, Identity, and Access Errors**\n- **REGISTRY_ACCESS_DENIED**: "PermissionDenied", "Access denied", "does not have permission", "PERMISSION_DENIED", "AccessDeniedException"\n  - Fix: Grant permissions (USE_CATALOG, USE_SCHEMA, EXECUTE, SELECT) to endpoint service principal. Check resource ownership.\n- **SECRET_ACCESS_DENIED**: "Secret access denied", "secret scope PERMISSION_DENIED"\n  - Fix: Grant READ permission on secret scope to endpoint service principal or workspace\n- **PRIVATE_REPO_ACCESS_DENIED**: "HTTP Error 401", "Authentication failed", "private repository denied"\n  - Fix: Configure pip credentials in environment variables or use Databricks secret scope\n- **NETWORK_EGRESS_BLOCKED (SSL/Certificate)**: "SSL certificate verify failed", "CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED", "SSLError", "certificate invalid"\n  - Fix: Cannot verify SSL certificate for external service. Check corporate proxy settings or custom CA certificates.\n- **NETWORK_EGRESS_BLOCKED (DNS)**: "getaddrinfo failed", "Name or service not known", "DNS lookup failed", "Could not resolve hostname"\n  - Fix: Cannot resolve hostname. Check DNS configuration, network policies, or verify hostname spelling.\n- **NETWORK_EGRESS_BLOCKED (Network)**: "Network unreachable", "No route to host", "Connection refused", "Network blocked", "Firewall blocked"\n  - Escalate: Network policy blocks external access. Contact workspace admin to allow egress to required services.\n- **IDENTITY_MISCONFIGURATION (Service Principal)**: "service principal invalid", "identity misconfigured", "Token expired", "Invalid token"\n  - Escalate: Check service principal is valid and has required permissions. Verify token configuration. Contact admin if persists.\n\n**Category E: Quota, Capacity, and Non-Actionable User Errors**\n- **QUOTA_EXHAUSTED**: "GPU quota exceeded", "vCPU quota"\n  - Escalate: Contact Databricks support to request quota increase\n- **CAPACITY_SHORTAGE**: "InsufficientInstanceCapacity"\n  - Escalate: Try different instance type or contact support for alternative regions\n- **INFRASTRUCTURE_LIMIT**: "Infrastructure limit reached"\n  - Escalate: Requires Databricks infrastructure team assistance\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- Multiple categories may appear in same deployment (e.g., dependency conflict + OOM)\n- HIGH confidence diagnoses should be acted on immediately\n- MEDIUM/LOW confidence may require additional investigation\n- Always check "Escalate to Support" flags in tool output\n'}}]);
